A||N||17||Fiero5||A couple of interesting pics ||||6||
Z||000000||Fiero5||05-04-2001||10:55 AM||||The first is of my daughter Tarrah. She loves her brothers new 85GT.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Tarrah_&_her_brothers_85_GT.JPG"> <BR>The next is when I stopped at a local gas station yesterday, and realized that all 4 cars were red. Thought that was kinda cool. The one in the right hand back was a beautiful buffed down Grand Am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/4_red_cars_getting_gas.JPG"> <P>Steve<P>||||reg||6
Z||000001||Cheever2||05-04-2001||12:36 PM||||Looks like Frasier's dad there wasn't too impressed with your 2-seater, sunroof & high wing.  Guess it was almost too much excitement for him just to get a red car.  Oh yeah, he was probably depressed from the gas prices.  He shouldn't put the gas cap on the car like that.  And where's your front license plate, mister?<P>Here's a thought: did anyone here ever coat the pump handle with Vasolene before leaving?  Me neither.  <p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 05-04-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000002||Fiero5||05-04-2001||12:57 PM||||Front license plate? On an aero nose?<BR>I dont think so.<P>I have a pending case that I filed with Concord NH (home of the NH division of motor vehicles), to allow any of our Fieros with aero noses exemption from needing a front plate.<P>"It impedes the air flow and causes needless over heating problems due to the restriction of the front air intake. The front plate and bracket also causes poorer gas mileage and more exhaust ejection causing uneeded.." yada, yada.<P>Steve||||reg||12
Z||000003||Cheever2||05-04-2001||02:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero5:<BR><B>...pending case that I filed, ...to allow any of our Fieros with aero noses exemption from needing a front plate.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>More power to ya, but you know what they'll say: "Then put it somewhere other than in front of the radiator".  Yeah, I know where to put it alright.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero5||05-04-2001||02:58 PM||||Some states do not require a front plate, so it isn't like it causes any harm or anything not having one. My Dad hasn't had one on his 87 GT since he got it many moons ago.<P>We just had a similar case here in NH, where this woman and her boyfriend who are a members of a car club we are in, tinted the windows on her Camaro. The cops snagged her and gave her a fix it ticket. They told her next time they see her, the tint had better be off. So this guy calls Concord and got a letter of exemption as they had told the director of motor vehicles that the bright car lights at night bothered her eyes and gave her headaches. If they can get one, so can I!<P>When I get my letter of exemption for not having to have a stupid plate on our aero nose Fieros, I will scan it and post it here on Pennocks.<P>Steve||||reg||12
Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||05-04-2001||03:13 PM||||Am I the only one that has figure out the gascap goes under the pump handle lever, to keep the pump on while you warsh your windshied, check your oil, or just lean against the car and look cool while the pump fills the tank and shuts off automatically?<P>  My 2000 saturn has the gas cap attached with a short cord, so I keep a tennis ball in the drivers door cup holder, works just as well.<P>  In fact, I have only seen two other people stick the gas cap under the pumphandlelever in about the last 10 years.<P>  BTW steve, you sure are posting alot of pictures of that red 86 lately, I hope you are not PO's that i didnt buy it (but everytime i see another picture of it, Im starting to wish maybe I had).<P>  I paid a little more for my 85 SE than you wanted for yours, but as soon as I:<P>  Finish replaceing the front brake caliper<BR>  get the ebrake cable freed up <BR>  get inspected<BR>  replace the shocks<BR>  solve whatever it is that is making my V6 run super rich<BR>  replace the heater core<BR>  get the AC working<BR>  get the yellow clearcoat off the alum wheels and polish them up<BR>  replace my CAT<BR>  check and see if my front exhaust manifold is cracked<BR>  find an engine cover sans luggage rack<BR>  and get the car painted<P>  then my car will be almost as good yours  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  I am having more fun fixing this car up than I ever had working on anything else, and my son is learning a lot in the process, but I do regret that I didnt get to meet you and see your collection.<P>  -Ken||||reg||1
Z||000006||JSocha||05-04-2001||03:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero5:<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Window tint, you can get a "Medical" exemption from a doctor if he deems (and of course if the individual can prove to the doctor) that any bright lights effect the individual while driving (Sun, headlights, etc. causing skin rashes, Migrains, etc.) <P>"...you see officer, I'm a Vampire and the sun really raises havok on my light skinned complexion.  Here is my coronors exemption ticket for my medical condition."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>The licence plate on the front of a vehicle I could never figure out as I always have gotten pulled over with the officer behind me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">, who, in their infinate wisdom, once they discover that I have no licence plate on the front will always state "I am unable to read your licence plate on the front."<P>Duhhhhhhh!  Officer!  "Well, that's because there is no licence plate on the front!" <P>&lt;inner thought process going on at the same time, you're behind me reading that plate...or...is there suddenly a good novel attached to my car (in licence plate form) that I am unaware of and you decided to read the ending first and then find out what happens in the beginning&gt;  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jnjsochasig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fiero5||05-04-2001||03:43 PM||||Ken, I am not POed at all. It sounds like it actually worked out better for you getting that other one. You are having more fun rebuilding that one with your son, than you probably would have had getting my 86. My 86 doesn't really need anything. Unless you wanted to mod it up or go to a V6, and swapping to a 2.8 could be done in a day.<P>You are seeing lot's of pictures of it lately (and some others soon) because I am currently driving this one around now. Though I have Fiero1 today. Still love that baby, especially since it was my first. I am sure that Fiero1 thru 6 have kinda been exposed alot and I am sure people would like to see some different ones of ours from time time. Fiero7 thru 12 should be getting more exposure this year since most of them are fairly new.<P>Steve||||reg||6
Z||000008||Ken Wittlief||05-04-2001||04:29 PM||||that reminds me, i should grab my daughters digital camera and get some 'before' pictures of my 85SE, before i start cleaning up the wheels and the other easy stuff.<P>  No point in me posting them though, till I get the car painted at least, unless nobody on here has ever seen a stock 85SE||||reg||1
