Z||000010||Pontiaddict||05-04-2001||06:12 PM||||Ken, most new gas pumps have a little lever on them that holds the pump handle for you. <BR>No gas cap needed.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fiero5||05-04-2001||06:21 PM||||Yeah, without the flex agent it will just flake off or sometimes depending on the paint, it won't even stick. You have to clean everything realy, realy good too!<P>Steve||||reg||1
Z||000012||mope||05-04-2001||06:34 PM||||i was told that the front licence plate was there so the cops have a better radar speed on you, it insures them that the radar/laser beam will have a perfect and reflective surface to clock you with.<P>but if that is the case i think im gunna go and bend my plate.<P>mope<P>------------------<BR>=======================<P>-= Silver 86 GT, being restored, and following major things to be done: Mr. Mike's Leather, new steering wheel, paint repair, ebrake repair, take apart and clean everything! <A HREF="http://www.mastergraphics.cjb.net" TARGET=_blank>www.mastergraphics.cjb.net</A>  <A HREF="http://www.mope.cjb.net" TARGET=_blank>www.mope.cjb.net</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||FieroFanaticus2||05-04-2001||07:35 PM||||I got pulled over the other day while driving my fiero for going 7 miles over the speed limit.  While he was giving me a lecture about safe driving he also noticed that my front plate was not on the vehicle, and also noticed my 20% Tint.  I got a warning for the speeding, a five day notice to put the plate on, and was told I need to remove the tint.  SOOOO, I slowed it down a bit, turned my fuzz buster on, put the plate on the front and showed to the police department then removed it when I got home, and finished up the last of the tinting (drivers side window was without tint at time of warning).  I hope I don't get pulled over by that cop again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000014||Predator||05-04-2001||10:15 PM||||Lucky for us we still don't have the License plate in the front law here in Georgia. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000015||mrgone||05-05-2001||01:08 AM||||im from nova scotia, no front plates there.<BR>now i go to school in ontario where i got my fiero. ontario is crazy. stupid front plate law here.<P>however i do like the fact that when i got my licence transferred to ontario, it erased my old speeding ticket, and i now have 0 demerits instead of 4||||reg||1
Z||000016||AusFiero||05-05-2001||01:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mope:<BR><B>i was told that the front licence plate was there so the cops have a better radar speed on you, it insures them that the radar/laser beam will have a perfect and reflective surface to clock you with.<P>but if that is the case i think im gunna go and bend my plate.<P>mope<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Don't know how true this is but an Australian cop with a Fiero was telling me they tried to clock his car with a police radar and it wouldn't give an accurate reading because the materials used in a Fiero absord a lot of the radar waves. We have stealth cars it seems if cops have certain equipment.<P>And I have gone way to fast past 5 radar traps and all the coppers seem to do is look at the car...look at their equipment then give it a shake. Haven't received a ticket ever in my Fiero but have in my wifes big chunky metal car.<P>Maybe we have different equipment over here?<P>||||reg||10
Z||000017||pontiacs4me||05-05-2001||03:32 AM||||I read somewhere on the net about a new paint system that is radar absorbant.  It is matte finish though.  If you clearcoat it, it will reflect back, so I guess if you have the desire to speed everywhere and you dont care if your car shines or not, its a good product for you.||||reg||1
